From 9f1ac1991e2de92c3c75bcd121ac544921066fdf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:16:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/24] Bind the swap horizon to its FIFO, and call a refused
 swap refused

The horizon a condemnation takes was a bare (channel, tail). A guest that
frees and redefines a FIFO after a GPU restart starts its heads again from
zero, so a swap published on the new incarnation, naming the same mapping
id and MappingInternal, still satisfied `tail - head > 0` against the old
tail and was consumed as if it had been cancelled.

A horizon is now each child FIFO's define generation, ring base page,
head and tail when the unwire was seen, and a present is judged by it only
if it is on the same incarnation and lies in [head, tail). DefineFifo and
FreeFifo bump the channel's generation and retire its horizons
(wire_guard_horizon_retired reason=define_fifo|free_fifo); a ring base
that no longer matches retires it too (reason=ring_changed).

A horizon taken when the drop is observed proves only that a present was
published before we looked, not that the guest cancelled that request. So
the branch no longer says it completes a cancelled swap: it refuses one
(wire_guard_swap_refused, how=refused). Refusing consumes the packet and
writes its completion stamp, because the stamp is the FIFO's command fence
and other packets wait on its slot; it does not retain the surface, does
not present it and raises no present event, so the guest sees the command
complete and no present happen. The doc on refuse_swap says which of those
is which.

process_root_packet is pub(crate) so the regression can free and define a
FIFO through the real handler: old tail 0x100, channel rebuilt, the new
swap at head 0 runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
